-- Independent tests, written from independent-expectations.md (scenario ids
-- in comments). Expected values come from that file, not from the encoding.

GIVETH A LIST OF DATE
`Matariki 2025-2027` MEANS LIST (Date 20 6 2025), (Date 10 7 2026), (Date 25 6 2027)

-- Field order of `Supply facts`: s105 applies, contrary s105(3), ending agreed in writing,
-- assigned, reason ceased, reason still continues, resumed as soon as reasonable, ceased knowingly.

-- S01 / S02 (both are "s 105 applies")
-- [Ported by the encoder: `Part 3 contravener` gained `in the course of producing a commercial gain` (s 80(3)(b)(i)), given as TRUE; no expected value changed.]
#ASSERT `the supply obligation continues` (`Supply facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, `supply has not ceased`, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE)
-- S03
#ASSERT NOT `the supply obligation continues` (`Supply facts` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, `supply has not ceased`, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE)
-- S04 / S06 / S07 (agreement in writing by the right people, or the Minister)
#ASSERT NOT `the supply obligation continues` (`Supply facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, `supply has not ceased`, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE)
-- S09
#ASSERT NOT `the supply obligation continues` (`Supply facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, `supply has not ceased`, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE)
-- S10
#ASSERT `the supply obligation is suspended` (`Supply facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, `(a) circumstances beyond the distributor's control`, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE)
-- S10 via the top-level goal
#ASSERT (`the distributor position for` (`Supply facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, `(a) circumstances beyond the distributor's control`, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE) `, scheme` (`Scheme facts` OF `a distributor`, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE) `, breach` (`Code breach` OF (Date 1 3 2024), (Date 1 3 2024), (Date 16 10 2026), FALSE, 0))'s `supply obligation suspended`
-- S11
#ASSERT `the supply obligation is suspended` (`Supply facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, `(b) safety, maintenance or upgrading`, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE)
-- S12
#ASSERT `the supply obligation is suspended` (`Supply facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, `(c) non-payment of money due for the place`, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE)
-- S13
#ASSERT NOT `the supply obligation is suspended` (`Supply facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, `(b) safety, maintenance or upgrading`, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE)
-- S14
#ASSERT NOT `the supply obligation continues` (`Supply facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, `supply has not ceased`, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE)
-- S15 (post-commencement agreement is not a s 105(3) agreement)
#ASSERT `the supply obligation continues` (`Supply facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, `supply has not ceased`, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE)

-- S18
#ASSERT `the distributor commits the s 105(4) offence` (`Supply facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, `(a) circumstances beyond the distributor's control`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE)
-- S19
#ASSERT NOT `the distributor commits the s 105(4) offence` (`Supply facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, `(a) circumstances beyond the distributor's control`, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE)
-- S21
#ASSERT `the distributor commits the s 105(4) offence` (`Supply facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, `another reason`, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE)
-- S22
#ASSERT NOT `the distributor commits the s 105(4) offence` (`Supply facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, `(b) safety, maintenance or upgrading`, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE)
-- S23
#ASSERT NOT `the distributor commits the s 105(4) offence` (`Supply facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, `(c) non-payment of money due for the place`, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE)
-- S24
#ASSERT NOT `the distributor commits the s 105(4) offence` (`Supply facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, `another reason`, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE)
-- S25
#ASSERT NOT `the distributor commits the s 105(4) offence` (`Supply facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, `another reason`, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE)
-- S26
#ASSERT `the most fine for the s 105(4) offence, days continuing` 0 EQUALS 10000
-- S27
#ASSERT `the most fine for the s 105(4) offence, days continuing` 10 EQUALS 20000
-- S28
#ASSERT `the most fine for the s 105(4) offence, days continuing` 365 EQUALS 375000

-- S30
#ASSERT `the earliest day for alternative supply after notice on` (Date 1 1 2026) AT MOST Date 1 1 2027
-- S31
#ASSERT NOT `the earliest day for alternative supply after notice on` (Date 1 1 2026) AT MOST Date 1 6 2026
-- S32
#ASSERT `the earliest day for alternative supply after notice on` (Date 1 1 2026) AT MOST Date 2 7 2026
-- S33 (ambiguous boundary; reading in expectations: 1 Jul 2026 is too early)
#ASSERT NOT `the earliest day for alternative supply after notice on` (Date 1 1 2026) AT MOST Date 1 7 2026
-- S34
#ASSERT `the earliest day for alternative supply after notice on` (Date 31 8 2026) AT MOST Date 1 3 2027
-- S35
#ASSERT NOT `the earliest day for alternative supply after notice on` (Date 31 8 2026) AT MOST Date 28 2 2027

-- D01
